{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/fakeLabel","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/lambda","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/lossFunction","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/penaltyStepSize","doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/WGANGP\/realLabel"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class","title":"WGANGP","externalID":"s:6Neuron6WGANGPC","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WGANGP"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WGANGP","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Neuron"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A Wasserstein GAN with Gradient Penalty (WGAN-GP) trainer.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Neuron\/documentation\/Neuron\/GAN"],"kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WGANGP"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enforces the Lipschitz constraint by penalizing "},{"code":"λ · (‖∇ₓD(x̂)‖ − 1)²","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on samples "},{"code":"x̂","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolated between real and generated ones, instead of clipping weights."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The penalty’s gradient with respect to the critic’s parameters needs a second derivative,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"(∂\/∂θ ∇ₓD) · v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which Neuron’s first-order backward pass can’t produce. Mixed partials"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"commute, so it equals the change in the parameter gradient when the input moves along "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and one extra forward and backward pass at a perturbed input approximates it by finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differences. See "},{"code":"gradientPenalty(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The perturbed pass must see the same critic as the unperturbed one, so the critic must be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deterministic in training mode: no "},{"code":"Dropout","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A fresh mask in each pass would be divided by the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finite-difference step and swamp the penalty. "},{"code":"BatchNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" mixes samples, which the penalty"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a per-sample norm) assumes they don’t; use "},{"code":"LayerNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"GroupNormalize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a critic."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/neuron\/wgangp"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Neuron/documentation/Neuron/WGANGP/penaltyStepSize":{"url":"\/documentation\/neuron\/wgangp\/penaltystepsize","title":"penaltyStepSize","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"penaltyStepSize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tensor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIden